<title>FRANCE: CIC H1 net attrib 533 mln Fr, up 60.7 pct.</title>
<headline>CIC H1 net attrib 533 mln Fr, up 60.7 pct.</headline>
<dateline>PARIS 1996-10-01</dateline>
<text>
<p>Six months to june 30, 1996.</p>
<p>(Figures in millions of French francs unless stated)</p>
<p>    Net attributable			     533  vs	     332</p>
<p>    Net banking income			 8,562  vs	   8,156</p>
<p>    Operating costs			    6,474  vs	   6,437</p>
<p>    Operating result			   2,088  vs	   1,719</p>
<p>    Result before tax, FRBG		    926  vs	     675</p>
<p>    FRBG (general bank risk fund) payment  223  vs		47</p>
<p>    Pre tax result				 703  vs	     628</p>
<p>    Exceptional charge			    14  vs		18</p>
<p>    Tax						 94  vs	     243</p>
<p>    Solveny ratio (percent)		   5.18  vs	    5.20</p>
<p>Provisioning breakdown:</p>
<p>		   various			    51  vs		42</p>
<p>		   operating		     1,286  vs	     989</p>
<p>		   property values		+170  vs		-9</p>
<p>		   property sales		   +5  vs		-4</p>
<p>NOTE - CIC bank, which is part of state-controlled insurer GAN and about to be privatised, issued the results in a statement.</p>
<p>-- Paris Newsroom +33 1 4221 5452</p>
</text>
